\section{Party-specific contrasts and sensitivity analyses}
\label{sec:oa-party}
The baseline model pools the appearance-associated inequality across parties. The party-specific specification in \autoref{eq:party-model} allows the cue association and gender intercept to differ across parties. Table~\ref{tab:oa-party} reports the corresponding one-SD contrasts from the full municipality-clustered covariance matrix. Candidate and municipality counts describe the observations available within each party--gender cell. Inference uses the pooled model's \Sexpr{party_model_clusters} municipality clusters.

Because individual intervals do not test a common slope across parties, we also test whether the atypicality slopes are equal within each gender, using the full municipality-clustered covariance matrix. The joint test gives \Sexpr{party_test_summary("All genders")}. The corresponding tests within men and women give \Sexpr{party_test_summary("Men")} and \Sexpr{party_test_summary("Women")}, respectively. \Sexpr{party_heterogeneity_text}

