\section{Sensitivity analyses}
\label{sec:oa-sensitivity}
The pooled inequality may also depend on the comparison setting, target sample, and restrictions on control coefficients. Table~\ref{tab:oa-sensitivity} varies these features. Municipality-by-party fixed effects restrict comparisons to candidates on the same local party list. Singleton lists consequently do not identify cue slopes. To assess dependence on candidates with unusually many votes, upper-tail exclusions remove \Sexpr{paper_values$n_trim1_removed} candidates above the \Sexpr{100-paper_values$trim_percent[1]}th percentile and \Sexpr{paper_values$n_trim5_removed} above the \Sexpr{100-paper_values$trim_percent[2]}th percentile. These exclusions change the candidate population represented by the estimate. Finally, separate-gender models allow all coefficients, including the control associations, to differ between men and women.

